cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Pan-genome and selection analysis of 290 Capripoxvirus genomes
message: If you use this repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tabashiri
    given-names: Raana
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7975-6686'
    affiliation: >-
      Zurich University of Applied Sciences (ZHAW)
repository-code: 'https://github.com/RaanaT1375/capripoxvirus-pangenome'
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pipeline and results for a pan-genome, phylogenetic,
  recombination and selection analysis of 290 Capripoxvirus genomes
  (240 lumpy skin disease virus, 34 sheeppox virus, 16 goatpox virus).
  The principal result is a McDonald-Kreitman estimate of adaptive
  amino-acid divergence on the LSDV branch (alpha = 0.604), together with
  a quantitative demonstration of why codon substitution models are not
  applicable within present-day LSDV.
keywords:
  - lumpy skin disease virus
  - Capripoxvirus
  - pan-genome
  - molecular evolution
  - McDonald-Kreitman test
  - positive selection
license: MIT
